> what about controllers not defined as services?

The compiler pass can only process definitions that are registered in the ContainerBuilder. If a class is not discovered in this way, it will not be included in your compiler pass or with the `registerAttributeForAutoconfiguration`.

The only requirement if that the service definition has "autoconfiguration" enabled, which is the default config for new Symfony applications. Moreover, controllers should have "autoconfiguration" enabled [to](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/7278aa035af69b83d398b7220669ecb61be5a639/src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/DependencyInjection/FrameworkExtension.php#L696-L697) [get](https://github.com/symfony/symfony/blob/7278aa035af69b83d398b7220669ecb61be5a639/src/Symfony/Bundle/FrameworkBundle/DependencyInjection/FrameworkExtension.php#L769-L774) the `controller.service_arguments` tag.
